- Will the money last? now says what the answer rests on: a line under the answer counts the numbers that are yours, our guesses and usual figures and names what is not counted yet, and the one filled button under the answer, "Check the numbers behind this ↓", opens a card that shows the three numbers that matter most (the rest one tap away: the money left over, the match, what goes into the 401(k), spending, Social Security, when you stop, growth, prices) with what one change would do to the age the money runs out; coming back after a change says "Before your change ... Now ..."; a "Go deeper" card links to Could you stop sooner?, the chance the money lasts, What matters most, two plans side by side and history; Retirement settings open on the spending figure and Save, the other six under "More settings", which says "1 to save" while it holds a figure not saved yet.
